[
  {
    "id": 4641122105,
    "body": "Corrected in 53c767a0. The decision tree now has a No branch from K: customer data only, the processor notice is already sent, SurveyBeat does not file Art. 33(1), and the customer Controller decides Art. 34. That path still logs the §6.4 register."
  },
  {
    "id": 4641122111,
    "body": "Corrected in 53c767a0. Triage (T+2h to T+6h) starts the Art. 34 assessment when high risk is already apparent. The T+24 to T+48 window only finishes an assessment that was not already clear. P1 still says assess immediately."
  },
  {
    "id": 4641122114,
    "body": "Corrected in 53c767a0. The runbook now runs `pnpm test:preview-privacy --stage production https://dashboard.surveybeat.app https://submit.surveybeat.app` with `CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN` and `CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID` set. `canary-sweep.ts` exits 2 without `--stage`, both Worker URLs, and those variables."
  },
  {
    "id": 4641122128,
    "body": "Corrected in 53c767a0. Containment is to remove or empty `OPENROUTER_API_KEY`. `OpenRouterAiClient` returns `AiNotConfigured` only when the key is missing or empty. A rotated non-empty key still sends."
  },
  {
    "id": 4641122148,
    "body": "Corrected in 53c767a0. R-01 now says `participation` is `(round_id, person_id)` and is structurally separate from `submission`. `submission` and `answer` are the tables with no person column."
  },
  {
    "id": 4641122156,
    "body": "Corrected in 53c767a0. R-05 now says Question text is not redacted, so a name typed into a Question is sent. Comment name redaction uses email local parts, because `person` has no display-name column. This change narrows the record. It does not add redaction of Question text."
  },
  {
    "id": 4641122159,
    "body": "Corrected in 53c767a0. R-07 now includes `GET /delivery?token=` and `GET /api/reminders/unsubscribe?t=` (issue #311). Residual risk on that path is Medium until #311. The answer-link fragment is `#t=`."
  },
  {
    "id": 4641122165,
    "body": "Corrected in 53c767a0. Section 3 no longer treats every stored comment as non-personal data. A comment that identifies its author through a unique anecdote stays personal data for retention and for rights requests. The structural split (no Person column) is what the tests show."
  },
  {
    "id": 4641122173,
    "body": "Corrected in 53c767a0. The fragment claim is limited to answer links (`#t=`). `GET /delivery?token=` and `GET /api/reminders/unsubscribe?t=` still send the token on the query string (issue #311)."
  },
  {
    "id": 4641122179,
    "body": "Corrected in 53c767a0. The OpenRouter row now says Question text is not redacted, and that name redaction uses email local parts. No product change in this docs pull request."
  },
  {
    "id": 4641122183,
    "body": "Corrected in 53c767a0. The LIA now says `redact` removes email local parts from the roster. `recordFirstAnswer` passes `dirState.people`, and `PersonRecord` has email and no display name, so a display name that is not in a local part is not removed."
  },
  {
    "id": 4641122198,
    "body": "Corrected in 53c767a0. The LIA separates upstream `zdr: true` from OpenRouter's own screening. OpenRouter may retain content flagged as potential CSAM, including ZDR traffic, and reported material is kept for one year (research note §6, 18 U.S.C. § 2258A)."
  },
  {
    "id": 4641122204,
    "body": "Corrected in 53c767a0. The 30-day backup window is limited to the in-app Privacy page (`privacy.restore`). The LIA now describes the Invitation and answer-page sentences the product actually renders, including the AI notice only when `ai_processing` is on."
  },
  {
    "id": 4641122211,
    "body": "Corrected in 53c767a0. `directory.removePerson` sets `person.removed_at` and `membership.ended_at`. It deletes `person_index`, `participation`, and `test_send`, and revokes Invitations. The person row and membership history stay. There is no automated purge of that row."
  }
]

