{
  "tool_name": "t3-code__delegate_task",
  "tool_input": {
    "title": "Re-review PR 321 head",
    "role": "review",
    "isolation": "worktree",
    "mode": "async",
    "clientRequestId": "review-321-neon-5",
    "target": {
      "providerInstanceId": "antigravity",
      "model": "gemini-4-neon",
      "options": { "thought_level": "high" }
    },
    "task": "Review pull request 321 in chrisdoc/surveybeat-next. Read only. Do not edit files, commit, push, merge, comment on GitHub, or spawn subagents. Do not run the unit test suite or Organization.test.ts; ports 1337 and 1338 may be in use by another worktree.\n\nThe branch is t3/gdpr-313-compliance-pack. The commit to review is exactly 6d12ff5e251c1c02985c2a425003d7daef5f445d. Fetch origin and check out that commit. Run git rev-parse HEAD and refuse to review if it is any other SHA. Neon review-321-neon-4 approved only 1de1aae3a0a4ebc82da420591a3a9c790faa6abc. That approval does not cover 6d12ff5e.\n\nThis is a docs-only GDPR pack: docs/compliance/ropa.md, dpia.md, breach-response-runbook.md, vendor-dpa-register.md, plus a pointer in docs/infra.md. No product code changes belong in this PR.\n\nReview the diff from 1de1aae3 to 6d12ff5e against the code, and spot-check that the earlier corrections were not reverted.\n\nClaims that must match the code:\n1. Redaction.ts: extractCandidateNames splits email local parts only on `.`, `_`, and `-`, and skips a normalized candidate shorter than 2 characters. Intl.Segmenter word breaks at `+` and `%`, so those characters are not candidate splits. A local part such as abc+def from abc+def@example.com can remain in a comment. EMAIL_PATTERN still replaces a full email address. person has no display-name column. The docs may say this in ropa.md section 3, dpia R-04 and R-05, and vendor-dpa-register.md (OpenRouter row and the LIA store-time bullet). They must not claim every local part is removed.\n2. ropa.md section 3 heading is \"Anonymity and residual identifiability of submission and answer rows (GDPR Recital 26)\". It must not say every stored row is non-personal data. The section body must still say a unique anecdote can identify the author and is then personal data for retention and rights.\n3. breach-response-runbook.md: T+2h to T+6h starts the Art. 34 assessment when high risk is already apparent, continues it as evidence arrives, and finishes it without undue delay, and says not to wait until T+24. T+24h to T+48h finishes an assessment that started at triage and is still open, and also finishes one that triage did not already show as high risk. Do not collapse those two rows into a single moment.\n4. Still true, and must not have been reverted: the opt-out write is POST /api/reminders/unsubscribe (RFC 8058 List-Unsubscribe-Post); GET /api/reminders/unsubscribe only renders the confirmation page. GET /delivery?token= and GET /api/reminders/unsubscribe?t= still send the live token (issue 311) and R-07 residual stays Medium until that is fixed. Answer links use #t=. Stored submission and answer rows have no Person column, which is not a Recital 26 conclusion that every comment is non-personal. Person-row erasure is not available (removePerson does not DELETE FROM person). EMAIL_DEAD_LETTERED logs sendId and the send state tag, not an error code.\n\nGlossary: Pulse, Person, Round, Submission, Answer, Invitation, Edit key, Organization, Team, Lead. Do not require the docs to say User, Response, or Respondent.\n\nReturn APPROVE only if every claim above is accurate on 6d12ff5e. Otherwise REQUEST CHANGES and quote the inaccurate sentence with the file and the code that contradicts it. Name the SHA you reviewed in the first line."
  }
}

